# sync_timedb queue orchestrator contract

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

Production coordinator for `sync_timedb` is **`run_sync_timedb_queue_orchestrator`** (wired from `run_sync_timedb_supervisor_from_parsed`). The B supervisor loop / `ArchiveJanitor` tick coordinator are **retired** — do not dual-run orchestrators.

## Laws

| Law | Detail |
|-----|--------|
| One process / `archive_dir` | Exclusive flock on `{archive_dir}/.sync_timedb_orchestrator.fnctl.lock` |
| Job kinds | Redis `job:v1`: ingest ZSET (hot/catchup ranges), append/discover/day_close LISTs, `SET NX EX` leases with **OQ-1 EX = per-file timeout max (default 86400) and no coordinator heartbeat renew**, in-flight HASH, path-only lease identity + payload fingerprint; dead-owner steal must requeue inflight |
| Atomic claim | Lua claim (ranged pop + SET NX + in-flight) / LIST claim; never `ZREM`/`LPOP` then lease. Fill paths must not call `pop_ingest_job_ranged` / `pop_list_job` |
| Reaper / steal | Tick `reap_expired_inflight`; boot **and** rate-limited runtime `steal_dead_owner_leases` **plus** `reconcile_this_owner_orphan_leases` when `len(local) < pool` and ingest ZSET is deep (SCAN, never KEYS) — not only when local maps are empty; host+boot scoped owner tokens; this-owner orphan leases (no local Future) are requeued |
| Streaming submit | Discover → `ZADD` as paths arrive; never wait for full find to finish before first enqueue; stop at ingest queue cap |
| Calendar day | Discover resolves day from the daily tar path; **do not** substitute today. Unresolved day → skip ingest enqueue |
| Reserved ingest slots | `hot_cap = max(1, (2*pool)//3)`, `catchup_cap = pool - hot_cap` (catchup floored to 1 when `pool >= 2`). Catchup may use unused pool slots when the hot range is empty **or** when free slots remain after hot→cap / reserved catchup / hot spillover — elevated hot retry then catchup with `catchup_dispatch_cap(..., hot_submitted=0)` (**RC7**: do **not** require `hot_submitted==0` this tick). While hot still submits into reserved/spillover passes, reserved `catchup_cap` holds for that earlier pass |
| Redis HLEN capacity (**RC8**) | Redis ingest inflight **HLEN** is pool-capacity authority; local `ingest_inflight` maps are a cache. When `zcard>0` and (`HLEN < pool` or `len(local) > HLEN`), reconcile/prune phantoms missing from Redis inflight+lease (never prune live Redis holders). Hygiene must **not** skip solely because `len(local) >= pool` when Redis is underfull. Band caps use maintained `hot_used`/`catchup_used` counters (no per-claim full-map walk). Claim EVAL returns fingerprint (RC8b); multi-claim batch (RC8c); steal uses per-identity `HGET` not `HGETALL` (RC8d); 0-submit deep-ZSET ticks sleep `<<50ms` (RC8e); census is pipelined `zcount+zcount+zcard` |
| Reband | Recompute band at claim time and `ZADD` the same identity with the new score **plus** `LEASE_CONFLICT_SCORE_PENALTY` (RC9: deprioritize reband ping-pong) |
| Ingest tick order | ingest-coordinator: **fill → drain → fill** (same tick) so completions refill before sleep; then reap / idle poll |
| Populate pool | Orchestrator starts `PopulatePoolController` **before** boot discover submit, `reap_and_restart` each tick, `stop` on exit |
| Boot discover | After steal/reap and **after** ingest-pool + `populate.start()`, enqueue discover identity and `_submit_background_discover` (same executor as idle reconstruct). Log `queue_orchestrator boot discover submitted` **only after** `_submit_background_discover` returns. MainThread must **not** call `_boot_stream_discover` synchronously before the fill loop — that inlines sealed populate when the controller is still None (hpcperfstats03 2026-08-25: 13h `[main]` sealed `populate_source=*`, zero ingest-pool) |
| Discover bg Lock | `_submit_background_discover` creates the `ThreadPoolExecutor` and `submit`s **under one** `_discover_bg_lock` hold. **Never** call `_discover_executor()` while holding that lock — `_discover_bg_lock` is a non-reentrant `threading.Lock()`; nesting deadlocks MainThread forever (hpcperfstats03 2026-08-26: py-spy idle at `_discover_executor` under submit; discover LIST LLEN=1; fill never starts) |
| MainThread allowlist | MainThread does **pool/thread maintenance only**: flock, boot steal/reap once, create pools, `populate.start()` / `reap_and_restart()`, start subsystem threads, boot discover submit, **pause-protocol** ingest pool recycle via `AtomicPoolRef`, fail-closed on unexpected coordinator death, shutdown `draining`→`drained` barrier. **Forbidden on MainThread:** `_fill_*`, `_drain_*`, `_idle_reconstruct_pass`, classify/find, `apply_async` |
| Subsystem ownership | One titled thread per kind: `ingest-coordinator` (ingest fill/drain/abandon + kind-scoped ingest reap + recycle request), `append-coordinator` (append fill/drain + **tar-deduped cheap day_close**; drain must honor `ArchiveAppendOutcome` gate-skip handoff + soft_requeue requeue), `day-close-coordinator` (day_close fill/drain into workers), `discover-bg` (unchanged Lock law), `reconstruct-coordinator` (idle reconstruct + census + **kind-scoped discover reap**; no discover submit while discover-bg busy). Fix every flaw **only** in the owning subsystem |
| Ingest recycle pause | ingest-coordinator sets `recycle_requested` + `paused`, requeues local claims, stops `apply_async`; MainThread recycles and publishes via `AtomicPoolRef`; then clears pause. Never terminate the pool from a fill thread while another thread may `apply_async`. **Submit-age wall-clock abandon watchdog is retired** — do not reclaim slots from `submitted` age; idle-stall + statement_timeout own give-up |
| Bare drain TimeoutError | `_drain_ingest_ready` must **not** soft-requeue bare `TimeoutError` (no stage/elapsed); leave local inflight maps (H7). Soft-requeue packed `outcome=timeout` / rich escapes only |
| Lock sidecars | Discover skips `*.fnctl.lock`; fill ACK-drops claimed lock identities |
| Idle stall soft-kill | `sync_ingest_stall_idle_s` (default 1800); wall B floor default `0`; no coordinator watchdog fallback |
| Fail-closed death | Unexpected coordinator thread death → log + `os._exit(1)` (or injected exit). **No** silent restart with empty local inflight maps |
| Kind-scoped reaper | Each coordinator calls `_reap_stale_inflight(kinds=(own,), skip_identities=local maps)`. Boot may still reap all kinds once before threads start. `reconstruct-coordinator` reaps `JOB_KIND_DISCOVER` only |
| Append gate-skip drain | When append worker returns `ArchiveAppendOutcome(gate_skipped=True, skipped_paths=…)`, `_drain_append_ready` must `_handoff_retryable_paths_to_ingest` **before** `ack_job` — never ACK-drop uningested paths. `soft_requeue` → `requeue_job` without ACK |
| Cheap day_close | Append (and reconstruct daily-dir scan) enqueue via `enqueue_cheap_day_close_if_needed` (`filesystem_complete=False`, **find-free basename min-age gate**); Redis LIST dedupe keeps ≤1 queued/inflight per tar. Full remaining-raw find only on day_close **workers**. Do not RPUSH days younger than `sync_day_close_min_age_hours` |
| Append fill skip | `_fill_append_slots`: missing path / empty identity / unresolved daily tar → **`ack_job` (drop)** with `APPEND_FILL_SKIP_BUDGET` (same magnitude as ingest). Do **not** unbounded `requeue`+`continue` for impossible identities. Claim into **day-keyed** in-memory lists (`YYYY-MM-DD`); mixed FIFO **does not break** the fill on the first other-tar item. Same-tar inflight holds claims in the day list (no second writer). Empty day keys are deleted. Partial batch only when Redis LIST is exhausted |
| Union rewrite | `rebuild_daily_tar_member_union_in_place` copies with **named GNU tar extract** (`tar -x` / `zstd -d -c` pipe) and dest `tar -c`/`-r`. **Forbidden** on this path: per-name `tarfile.getmember` and dest `tarfile.open(..., "w")`. Truncated-tar `tarfile` repair remains recovery-only after GNU `tvf` fails |
| Ingest fill skip (RC9) | `_fill_ingest_band`: `skip_missing` (not complete) and `skip_fp` → **bump attempt**; at max → dead-letter/ACK; else **penalty requeue** (`score + LEASE_CONFLICT_SCORE_PENALTY`), not same-score spin. Missing + complete → ACK (unchanged). Append fill still ACK-drops missing paths |
| Discover append skip-complete | `_boot_stream_discover` injects `jr.discover_append_is_complete` (open-tar + warm Redis HGET only; cold → enqueue append + fire-and-forget populate). Workers keep `raw_stats_path_needs_tar_append` / `populate_and_wait` |
| Redis eviction | Startup `assert_redis_queue_safety` **fails closed** on `allkeys-*`; accept `noeviction` or `volatile-*`. Queue keys are TTL-free |
| Streaming submit | Discover → `ZADD` as paths arrive; never wait for full find to finish before first enqueue |
| Sliding-window pools | Refill on completion; never join an entire batch before the next hop |
| Reserved ingest slots | `hot_cap = max(1, (2*pool)//3)`, `catchup_cap = pool - hot_cap` (catchup floored to 1 when `pool >= 2`). Catchup overflow: empty hot **or** unused slots after hot/spillover even when `hot_submitted>0` this tick (**RC7**; see reserved-slot law above) |
| No whole-key `ZPOPMIN` | Ranged pop only (else catchup starves) |
| Idle poll | `sync_pool_poll_timeout_s` when slots free **and ingest ZSET empty**; when ZSET is deep but unclaimable, ingest-coordinator uses **short** poll (`min(0.05, poll_s)`) |
| Empty Redis ≠ caught up | Reconstruct from disk + Timescale + marks; checkpoint `.sync_timedb_state.json` is **not** reconstruct SoT |
| Skip completes | Do not enqueue identities whose complete predicates are already true |
| day_close | Filesystem complete + `sync_day_close_min_age_hours` (default 32) after day end; threads (max `sync_day_close_max_inflight`); ingest/append stay spawn |
| Steal inflight | Dead-owner steal requeues **only when inflight HASH existed**; nil inflight deletes the lease and must not `RPUSH` a LIST duplicate |
| Marks before ACK | Spawn ingest worker and `--jid` persist file-complete / zero-host marks from the packed outcome **before** Redis ACK |
| No-arg CLI | `startdate=enddate=None` (whole archive hot+catchup); never default `days_to_process=5` |
| `deferred_age` / `incomplete_raw` | Cooperative day_close outcomes: requeue **without** bumping attempts. Drain **ACK only** `complete` (filesystem + min-age). Never ACK a no-op `sealed` while remaining raw exists |
| Non-blocking day_close slot | When day-close is only waiting on ingest/append/lock/restore/DB gate owned elsewhere → handoff, return cooperative ``yielded``, release lease, requeue **without** attempt bump. Do **not** hold a `sync_day_close_max_inflight` slot on a foreign-subsystem wait |
| Reconcile stall-confirm yield | During ``rebuild_daily_tar_member_union_in_place``, emit rate-limited ``queue_orchestrator day_close stage_progress … advancing=true|false``. Warn after **120s** continuous no ``members_done`` advance; cooperative ``yielded`` / ``reason=stall_confirmed`` only after **1800s** continuous no progress at a **safe checkpoint** between members. **Forbidden:** abort because total merge wall time is large while ``members_done`` still advances. Hang inside one named GNU tar extract cannot yield until that subprocess returns |
| Redis loop | Mid-loop Redis errors **fail closed** (raise/exit); never invent `hot_queued=1` |
| Production membership | Open-tar member maps via GNU `tar tvf` / `zstd` CLI — not Python `tarfile` empty-on-truncate |
| Persistence mismatch | Boot calls `ensure_persistence_contract(..., allow_reset=True)`: version mismatch resets registered sidecars + writes current contract (see `sync-timedb-persistence-contract.mdc`); never continue against mixed versions without reset |
| No persistence wipe on cutover | Do not bump contract / wipe sidecars as a *workaround* cutover (B-17); intentional version bumps still auto-reset on next boot |
| Anti-workaround | No dual CLI, no strangler wrapper of supervisor_loop, no janitor stall watchdogs as coordinator |
| Progress report | Every **600s** `reconstruct-coordinator` emits omit-zeros `queue_orchestrator progress day=` lines + one `status` footer (`sync_timedb_progress_report.py`). Prefer day tokens; parse day_close LIST identities from tar-path basename or `YYYY-MM-DD` (`day_token_from_day_close_identity`). Day-close tokens: `dc_run=` at fill, `complete=` on ACK, `incomplete_raw=` when remaining raw, `deferred_age=` / `yielded=` / `verify_failed=`; `sealed=` / `tar_delete=` only when those steps ran. Status holds Redis/process cross-cuts (`busy=` incl discover, orphan_inflight, q_delta, ingest_hot/catchup as current/queued). 60s census kept with `busy=` (replaces `local=I/A/D`); census ratios are **current/queued**. No INFO `queue_orchestrator idle reconstruct work=` — day `reconstruct_enq=` / `incomplete_seen=` own that visibility. Do not name a calendar-day token `day_close=` (status already uses `day_close=inflight/queued`). Day-close slot breadcrumbs: `day_close claim|vacate|stage_enter|stage_exit|stage_progress` (incl `advancing=` / `stall_confirmed`). **`fill_block=`** on status when ingest fill submits 0 while `len(local) < pool` and ZSET is deep (not only local-empty); clear when **Redis HLEN ≥ pool−1** (RC9: not merely when a tick submits >0). Under-capacity logs include `redis_hlen=` / `hot_used=` / `catch_used=` census |
| Archive job INFO | One INFO `archive_job_done` per job with `tar_bytes`/`members_source`/`mapped`/`to_add`/`appended`; begin/duty/`Archived batch`/successful redis merge are DEBUG-only |
| Gate-skip INFO | No INFO `Archive/delete gate: skipped` or `handoff_to_ingest … reason=gate_skip`; day-line `gate_skip=` / `ingest_handoff=` own visibility |

## Predicates (B-09)

- Discovered incomplete ingest → ingest job exists
- Remaining-raw incomplete → ingest and/or append job exists
- `day_close` complete = filesystem + 32h (manifest `phase=done` is not SoT)

